{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788202098,"nonce":"Qu89N4ts2z9dG8WUUXV+toJO9iw=","message":"VERIFICATION (backlog verification pass, git-bug 2f2796e, run fbb2c59)\n\nCORRECTED — one instruction in amendment #1 would, if followed literally, POLLUTE\nTHE SAVE on every call; one claim in amendment #5 is wrong about what the game\ngives you; and the acceptance has two bullets that cannot be satisfied today.\nEverything else in five amendments checks out, several with exact line agreement.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 1 — \"REPRODUCE `!entDef.IsResearchFinished`\" IS AN INSTRUCTION TO CALL\nA WRITE-ON-READ ACCESSOR, AND THE GUARDED ROUTE ALREADY EXISTS\n=====================================================================\n\nAmendment #1 is right that the gate is `RimWorld/Designator_Build.Visible` and\nthat `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt` has no research check — an unpiped grep\nfor `Research|TechLevel|techLevel` over the WHOLE of `Verse/GenConstruct.cs`\nreturns nothing at all. CONFIRMED, and stronger than stated.\n\nBut `Verse/BuildableDef.IsResearchFinished` loops\n`researchPrerequisites[i].IsFinished`; `ResearchProjectDef.IsFinished =\u003e ProgressReal \u003e= Cost`;\n`ProgressReal =\u003e Find.ResearchManager.GetProgress(this)`; and\n`RimWorld/ResearchManager.GetProgress` is:\n\n    if (progress.TryGetValue(proj, out var value)) { return value; }\n    progress.Add(proj, 0f);\n    return 0f;\n\n`progress` is `Scribe_Collections.Look`-scribed. So **`IsResearchFinished` inserts\na zero entry per unvisited prerequisite, into scribed state, every time it is\nread** — the exact accessor DESIGN's 2026-08-30 decisions entry names first in\nits list of four, and the one `Source/AutoRimmer/WorldSafe.cs` already documents\nat length and already replaces with `WorldSafe.Finished(ResearchProjectDef)`\n(\"`ResearchProjectDef.IsFinished`, without the insert\", gated by\n`WorldSafe.ResearchRefsOk`).\n\nThe amendment as written tells the worker to reproduce the vanilla clause\nverbatim. It should read: **reproduce the gate THROUGH `WorldSafe.Finished`.**\n(Same note applies on 3.6 / `48f666c`, where `RecipeDef.AvailableNow` bottoms out\nin the same method — see that issue's verification comment.)\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 2 — \"THE REPORT CARRIES THE GAME'S OWN REASON STRING\" IS WRONG FOR\n`DeconstructibleBy`, AND `Blockers.cs` ALREADY KNOWS BETTER\n=====================================================================\n\n`Verse/Building.DeconstructibleBy(Faction)` does return an `AcceptanceReport`, and\nit has NO overrides anywhere in the tree — but every rejection inside it is a\nbare bool. `!def.building.IsDeconstructible` is `return false;` with no string;\nthe fallback is `return ClaimableBy(faction);`, and `Building.ClaimableBy` yields\na reason only on its `FactionPreventsClaimingOrAdopting(..., out var reason)`\nbranch. So for the case that matters most — a mineable rock wall — the report is\nrejected WITH AN EMPTY REASON.\n\n`Source/AutoRimmer/Blockers.cs` states this correctly in its own header (\"a\nmineable rock wall is rejected by `DeconstructibleBy` with an EMPTY reason\") and\nguards it (`reason = string.IsNullOrEmpty(report.Reason) ? null : report.Reason;`).\nThe issue's amendment is the stale half. Two smaller inversions in the same\nparagraph: `DeconstructibleBy` runs the `CompForceDeconstructable()` loop FIRST\n(so a comp can accept a def whose `IsDeconstructible` is false), and the\namendment omits `if (DebugSettings.godMode) { return true; }`, which `Blockers.cs`\ndoes record.\n\n=====================================================================\nCORRECTION 3 — AMENDMENT #1's GATE LIST IS ONE CLAUSE OF SIX\n=====================================================================\n\n`Designator_Build.Visible` does contain `if (!entDef.IsResearchFinished) { return false; }`\nand a `maxTechLevelToBuild` check. It ALSO contains, and the amendment names\nnone of these:\n\n  * `if (DebugSettings.godMode) { return true; }` — the first clause, and the\n    legitimate bypass for instant/dev mode.\n  * `entDef.minTechLevelToBuild` (not only max).\n  * `entDef.minMonolithLevel \u003e Find.Anomaly.HighestLevelReached \u0026\u0026 Find.Anomaly.GenerateMonolith`.\n  * `if (!Find.Storyteller.difficulty.AllowedToBuild(entDef))`.\n  * a loop over `entDef.PlaceWorkers` calling `placeWorker.IsBuildDesignatorVisible(entDef)`.\n\nA `build` verb that reproduces only the research clause is still a god-hand for\nscenario- and difficulty-restricted defs. Given that this issue's own amendment\nis the one making the gate-lives-in-the-widget argument, it should carry the\nwhole widget.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONFIRMED, MEMBER BY MEMBER\n=====================================================================\n\n- Roof areas. `Verse/Room.Notify_RoomShapeChanged` -\u003e `Map.autoBuildRoofAreaSetter.TryGenerateAreaFor(this)`,\n  and `Verse/AutoBuildRoofAreaSetter.TryGenerateAreaNow` opens verbatim:\n  `if (room.Dereferenced || room.TouchesMapEdge || room.RegionCount \u003e 26 || room.CellCount \u003e 320 || room.IsDoorway) { return; }`\n  terminating in `map.areaManager.BuildRoof[item2] = true;`. CONFIRMED exactly.\n  TWO REFINEMENTS the amendment omits and both matter for the acceptance:\n  the room must NOT BE FOGGED (`!Fogged` is in the `Notify_RoomShapeChanged`\n  guard), and `TryGenerateAreaFor` only QUEUES (`queuedGenerateRooms.Add(room)`) —\n  `TryGenerateAreaNow` runs from `AutoBuildRoofAreaSetterTick_First`, i.e. NEXT\n  TICK. So the roof area does not exist synchronously after placement, and a test\n  that reads it in the same call will see nothing. Also, \"player-faction\" is\n  more specific than stated: EVERY border roof-holder must be player-faction-or-null\n  with `allowAutoroof`, and AT LEAST ONE must be player faction.\n  The 5x7 = 35 cells conclusion holds either way.\n- Install. `RimWorld/Designator_Install.CanDesignateCell` ends\n  `return GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt(PlacingDef, c, placingRot, base.Map, godMode: false, MiniToInstallOrBuildingToReinstall, ThingToInstall);`\n  and `DesignateSingleCell` branches to `PlaceBlueprintForInstall` /\n  `PlaceBlueprintForReinstall`. Same validator, different placement call, and note\n  the explicit `godMode: false`. CONFIRMED.\n- `ThingDef.IsNonDeconstructibleAttackableBuilding` composition — CONFIRMED\n  (source spells it as a guard chain ending `return building.draftAttackNonDeconstructable;`).\n  `Designator_Deconstruct.CanDesignateThing` returns the literal\n  `\"RemoveByAttackingTooltip\".Translate()` for exactly that case. CONFIRMED.\n- `Blockers.cs` exists and is already consumed by `SpatialVerbs`,\n  `DesignateEngine`, `DesignationVerbs`, `ZoneVerbs`, `AreaVerbs`, `DevVerbs` and\n  `PawnOrderVerbs`. CONFIRMED — the taxonomy is live, not aspirational.\n- Fog. All four observers do gate on `c.Fogged(map)`, and\n  `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt` independently rejects it with\n  `\"CannotPlaceInUndiscovered\"`. So `place-layout`'s preflight gets it twice.\n  CONFIRMED.\n- The glyph band. `Source/AutoRimmer/Spatial.cs`, class `CropRenderer`:\n  `private const string ReservedBand = \"?@$!\u0026^;\";` and `public const char FogGlyph = '?';`.\n  CONFIRMED verbatim.\n- \"AutoRimmer reads no catalog data at all (three comments, no code).\" CONFIRMED\n  exactly — three hits, all inside comment blocks in `Spatial.cs`.\n- `rimworld-tools/baseviz/ir.py` and `catalog.py` exist, `designs/` holds three\n  worked bases, and BetterBases is the XML dialect. CONFIRMED. Bearing on the\n  open questions: `ir.py` ALREADY carries `terrain` and `roof` grids, so \"IR\n  dialect delta (terrain? roof?)\" is partly answered before the worker starts.\n- Free layout primitives. `Building_SunLamp.MakeMatchingGrowZone` and\n  `Building_OrbitalTradeBeacon.MakeMatchingStockpile` do exactly what the\n  amendment says — but **both are `private`**, so \"both one call\" is wrong: the\n  mod replicates two lines each (`DesignatorUtility.FindAllowedDesignator\u003cDesignator_ZoneAdd_Growing\u003e()`\n  then `DesignateMultiCell(GrowableCells.Where(...))`) or reflects. `GrowableCells`\n  and `TradeableCells` ARE public, so the footprint really is free. And there is a\n  widget gate the amendment does not name: `DesignatorUtility.FindAllowedDesignator\u003cT\u003e() != null`\n  — both gizmos are hidden when it returns null.\n\n=====================================================================\nCONSISTENCY WITH `acee526` (WHICH DECLARES IT BLOCKS THIS)\n=====================================================================\n\nConsistent in intent, SILENT in text. 1adc737's Scope does say \"preflight EVERY\ncell first; on any failure: place NOTHING\" and its Invariants say \"No partial\nplacement without `--partial`\" — the same spirit. But it never names `acee526`,\nnever uses the word \"exact\", and never applies the rule to its own **instant\nmode**, which SPAWNS rather than blueprinting. `GenConstruct.CanPlaceBlueprintAt`\nis not the validator `GenPlace`/`GenSpawn` consult, so a clean preflight does not\nprevent a `ThingPlaceMode.Near` slide at spawn time. Instant mode is where the\n1.9 dependency actually bites, and this issue does not say so.\n\n(Side note for `acee526`'s author, recorded there too: an opt-in already exists\nunder the name `mode:\"direct\"`, and it is NOT exact-or-refuse — see that issue's\nverification comment.)\n\n=====================================================================\nACCEPTANCE — TWO BULLETS UNSATISFIABLE, ONE UNCOVERED GAP\n=====================================================================\n\n- **\"Room role=Bedroom\" WILL FAIL on a correctly built room.**\n  `RimWorld/RoomRoleWorker_Bedroom.GetScore` -\u003e `IsBedroom` -\u003e `IsBedroomHelper`\n  reads `bed.OwnersForReading`; an UNOWNED bed with `bed_emptyCountsForBarracks`\n  scores as BARRACKS. The acceptance never says a colonist must be ASSIGNED to\n  the bed, so a perfect 5x7 room reports `role: \"Barracks\"` and the bullet fails.\n  Add the assignment step — and note that assigning a bed owner is a verb the mod\n  does not have (see the `e1c072e` verification comment, which finds the same\n  gap from the prisoner side). Also: reading it is not free —\n  `Source/AutoRimmer/PlaceVerbs.cs` already documents that `Room.Role` and\n  `Room.GetStat` both run `UpdateRoomStatsAndRole()`.\n- **\"Same IR in instant mode -\u003e things-dump diff vs the built version is empty\n  (modulo construction byproducts)\" is UNTESTABLE TODAY, twice over.** (a) There\n  is no dump verb: `map dump --rect` belongs to 2.5 (`f7b6207`), which is still\n  open. Nothing to diff against. (b) \"modulo construction byproducts\" is\n  undefined, so \"empty\" is not a decidable predicate — a real diff always contains\n  rubble, filth, leftover stacks and frame residue, and nothing says which are\n  excused. Either take the 2.5 dependency explicitly or drop the bullet.\n- \"A deliberately colliding layout returns per-cell reasons and places nothing\" —\n  testable and well-supported. One gap: the acceptance does not require those\n  per-cell reasons to be in `Blockers`' `{removal, reason}` shape. Amendment #5\n  asks for it; the Acceptance does not. Say it where it will be measured.\n- **THE HIGHEST-VALUE REGRESSION TEST IN THE ISSUE IS UNWRITTEN.** Nothing in\n  Acceptance exercises \"attempt to `build` an unresearched def and get refused\" —\n  which is the entire subject of amendment #1. Add it, and add the tech-level and\n  difficulty variants from Correction 3 while you are there.\n\nAlso unresolved in the body: **amendment #2 asks for the acceptance to be\nadjusted (\"Adjust the acceptance so it demonstrates something the game was not\ngoing to do anyway\") and it was not.** The Scope still says \"blueprints + floor\ndesignations + roof areas\" and the Acceptance still reads as before. The issue and\nits own amendment disagree — same shape as 3.5's stale acceptance and 4.3's stale\ndependency line, and worth fixing in the body rather than only in a comment,\nsince the body is what a worker reads first.\n\n=====================================================================\nWHAT I AM INFERRING, NOT CONFIRMING\n=====================================================================\n\n- That `bed_emptyCountsForBarracks` is set on the beds a 5x7 acceptance would\n  place. I read the role worker's logic, not the def of whatever bed the layout\n  uses. The failure mode is real for the default case; check the specific def\n  before rewriting the bullet.\n- That instant mode is where 1.9 bites. That follows from the two validators\n  being different; I did not run instant mode.","files":null}]}